course: dictionary
lesson: 2194
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A couch is a long, soft seat that two or more people can sit on. Most people also call it a sofa. Many words have more than one meaning, so the words around them help you choose the right one. «Ordinary Romans ate bread, porridge, olives, cheese and vegetables, and rich Romans held feasts lying on couches, with dishes like dormice and fish sauce.» The clue is lying. People lay down on couches at feasts, so a couch must be something you can lie on.
explain: A doctor's couch is different from a family's couch. It is a long padded bed in a doctor's room, and you lie on it while the doctor checks you. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Couch can also be a verb, which means it is a doing word. Its meaning is formal: to express something in a certain way. Look for the clue in the sentence: «The letter was couched in polite words.» Polite words tell you how the letter was written. Couch potato is an informal phrase for someone who sits watching TV and does little exercise.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Couch» means a long, comfortable seat for two or more people; a sofa.
fact: «Couch» can also mean a long padded bed in a doctor's room, for lying on.
fact: «Couch potato» means a person who sits watching TV a lot and does little exercise.
fact: «Couched» (verb) means expressed in a certain way, as in «couched in polite words».
exercise: «The rich Romans held feasts lying on couches.» What is a couch? | A loud noise | *A long soft seat, like a sofa | A small room for cooking | A kind of dish served at feasts
exercise: Ravi says a couch potato is a vegetable. What is a couch potato? | A kind of vegetable | *Someone who sits watching TV and does little exercise | A very fast runner | A person who grows potatoes
exercise: «The letter was couched in polite words.» What does couched mean here? | Shouted loudly | *Expressed in a certain way | Hidden under a bed | Cooked slowly
test: In a doctor's room, what is the couch for? | To sit and read magazines | To store medicine | To keep the doctor's coat | *To lie on while the doctor checks you
test: «...rich Romans held feasts lying on couches.» Which word is the clue that a couch is something to lie on? | *lying | Romans | dishes | feasts
exam: Which sentence uses couch as a verb? | The sofa is green and soft. | He sleeps on the couch every night. | *The reply was couched in gentle words. | She sat on the couch to watch TV.
